<article class="env-definition" id="0BPZ">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BPZ">Definition <span data-tag="0BPZ">15.108.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a local ring. We say $A$ is <em>unibranch</em> if the reduction $A_{red}$ is a domain and if the integral closure $A'$ of $A_{red}$ in its field of fractions is local. We say $A$ is <em>geometrically unibranch</em> if $A$ is unibranch and moreover the residue field of $A'$ is purely inseparable over the residue field of $A$. </p>
</article>